meta {
  name: Get My Application
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/client/master-application
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

docs {
  # Get My Master Application

  The master profile attached to this account, in whatever state it is. This is
  the screen behind the "become a master" button: `data: null` means the form
  should be shown, anything else means the status should be.

  **Response 200 — never applied:**
  ```json
  { "data": null }
  ```

  **Response 200 — applied:**
  ```json
  {
    "data": {
      "id": 7,
      "status": "pending",
      "experience_years": 5,
      "about": "Работаю сантехником с 2019 года.",
      "rejection_reason": null,
      "reviewed_at": null,
      "has_access": false,
      "access_expires_at": null,
      "city": { "id": 1, "name": "Ашхабад" },
      "categories": [{ "id": 5, "name": "Замена труб" }],
      "created_at": "2026-08-15 10:00:00"
    }
  }
  ```

  **What each status means for the app:**

  | `status`   | Screen                                                        |
  |------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
  | `pending`  | "Under review" — the administrator has not decided yet        |
  | `approved` | Master mode; if `has_access` is `false`, the subscription is missing or expired |
  | `rejected` | Show `rejection_reason` and let them submit again              |

  `has_access` is the honest answer to "can this account work as a master right
  now": approved **and** not blocked **and** subscription still running.
}
